  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/dpv#organisational-measures-classes> .

<https://w3id.org/dpv#ManageConsent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>, <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Manage Consent"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Control for managing a given consent in terms of providing, reaffirming, or withdrawing it"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/dpv#ProvideConsent>, <https://w3id.org/dpv#WithdrawConsent>, <https://w3id.org/dpv#ReaffirmConsent> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://w3id.org/dpv#ProvideConsent>, <https://w3id.org/dpv#WithdrawConsent>, <https://w3id.org/dpv#ReaffirmConsent> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Indicates how the data subject can manage their consent in terms of providing it, or reaffirming or withdrawing a given consent. This concept is useful to represent a single location or interface where multiple controls are provided for consent"@en ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-12-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "accepted"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/dpv#> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/dpv#consent-controls-classes> .

