<https://w3id.org/dpv#PrimaryUse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>, <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class>, <https://w3id.org/dpv#ReuseCompatibility> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Primary Use"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Status indicating compatibility based on the use being either the original context or something that is compatible with it"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://w3id.org/dpv#ReuseCompatibility> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Primary Use refers to an assessment where two contexts are found to be compatible, e.g. if purpose is used to test compatibility, then for two activities the second activity is said be the primary use if its purpose is compatible with the first activity's purpose"@en ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2025-06-19"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-02-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
