<https://w3id.org/dpv#SecondaryUse> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>, <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class>, <https://w3id.org/dpv#ReuseCompatibility> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Secondary Use"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Status indicating incompatibility based on the use not being compatible with an earlier context"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://w3id.org/dpv#ReuseCompatibility> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Secondary Use refers to an assessment where two contexts are found to be incompatible, e.g. if purpose is used to test compatibility, then for two activities the second activity is said be the secondary use if its purpose is incompatible with the first activity's purpose"@en ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2025-06-19"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-02-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
