  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/dpv#physical-measures-classes> .

<https://w3id.org/dpv#Likelihood> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>, <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Likelihood"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The likelihood or probability or chance of something taking place or occurring"@en ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Likelihood can be expressed in a subjective manner, such as 'Unlikely', or in a quantitative manner such as \"Twice in a Day\" (frequency per period). The suggestion is to use quantitative values, or to associate them with subjective terms used so as to enable accurate interpretations and interoperability. See the concepts related to Frequency and Duration for possible uses as a combination to express Likelihood."@en ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2022-07-22"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "accepted"@en ;
  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> _:person-harshvardhan-j-pandit ;
  <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/example> <https://w3id.org/dpv/examples#E0068> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/dpv#> ;
  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/dpv#risk-classes> .

